    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1006">

                <pb facs="1164" n="1052" sameAs="frus:frus1935v03/pg1052"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">711.9421/48</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in Japan</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Grew</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 677</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1935-01-28">January 28, 1935</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: With reference to your despatch No. 1059 of
                    November 16, 1934,<anchor n="23" xml:id="d1006-f1"/> there is herewith
                    transmitted a preliminary draft of a proposed consular convention with
                        Japan.<anchor n="24" xml:id="d1006-f2"/> This draft was prepared in the
                    Department on the basis of the existing Treaty with Poland, signed at Washington
                    in 1931,<anchor n="25" xml:id="d1006-f3"/> and is in general similar to other
                    treaties concluded in recent years with Germany, Norway, Finland, Cuba and other
                    countries.</p>
                <p>This draft has not as yet received the approval of the Department and is
                    submitted to you at the present time for your confidential information and
                    study. It is requested that you examine the draft, referring the matter to the
                    Consul General, and report any suggestions or amendments that may appear
                    advisable.</p>
                <p>Very truly yours,</p>
                <closer>For the Secretary of State:<lb/><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">William
                            Phillips</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
